INFO:agent.loop:\u26a1 Executing tool: 'knowledge_agent' with arguments: {"source_title": "Ronin and Harmony Horizon bridge theft attribution and laundering evidence", "source_url": "SRC-001; SRC-002; SRC-003; SRC-004", "text": "SRC-001 (Elliptic, May 9 2023) reports that the FBI confirmed North Korea-backed Lazarus Group conducted the June 24 2022 Harmony Horizon Bridge exploit (~$99.7m). It says attribution was based on similarities to prior Lazarus blockchain laundering patterns; the funds were programmatically structured through Tornado Cash, mirroring the Ronin laundering method. It reports more than $555m sent through Tornado Cash from these hacks: over $468m from Ronin and $96m from Harmony; later funds were structured through Railgun, with about 70% of funds sent through Railgun estimated to be Harmony-related, and deposits into three exchanges, two of which (Binance and Huobi) announced blocking/seizing some funds. SRC-003 (Elliptic, Mar 29 2022, updated for Apr 14 OFAC sanctions) reports Ronin theft of 173,600 ETH and 25.5m USDC, worth $540m at theft; OFAC listed the thief Ethereum address owner as Lazarus Group. It reports 18% laundered by Apr 14: USDC swapped for ETH via DEXs, $16.7m ETH through three centralized exchanges, then $80.3m ETH through Tornado Cash, with $9.7m in intermediary wallets and $433m remaining in original wallet at that point. It says attack involved control of five of nine validator keys and that features mirrored prior Lazarus attacks. SRC-002 (Chainalysis, Sep 8 2022) reports Lazarus accessed five of nine Ronin validator keys, withdrew 173,600 ETH and 25.5m USDC, used over 12,000 addresses, and followed a typical five-stage laundering pattern: intermediary wallets, Tornado Cash mixing, ETH-to-BTC swap, Bitcoin mixing, crypto-to-fiat cashout; also chain-hopped ETH through BNB, swapped to USDD, and bridged to BitTorrent. It reports >$30m seized with law enforcement and industry cooperation, and that OFAC sanctioned Tornado Cash for laundering over $455m stolen from Axie Infinity. SRC-004 contains no substantive incident evidence in returned text."}
